# Anti-patterns

| Anti-pattern | Why it fails |
| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Whole-repo `lint --fix` during warn burn-down | Mass unrelated diff; blame noise |
| CI full-tree lint as only gate | Blocks on legacy; stalls teams |
| Docs without matching checks | Standards become suggestions |
| Ticket IDs in code comments | Rot when tooling changes |
| Cross-merging feature branches | Ratchet sees phantom "your" lines |
| Orchestrator implements code itself | Context blow-up; no separation of concerns |
| Subagent prose for simple lookups | Wastes parent context budget |
| Boy-scout uncapped | Every touch demands full file cleanup |
| `any` / untyped escape hatches in new code | Debt migrates forward |
| Secrets in repo "for local dev only" | Leak path to production |
| Plan-then-execute without backprop | Same bug class recurs; no contract memory |
| Multiple skills rewriting the same § | Drift; breaks sectioned ownership |
| Prose SPEC without `§` addressing / concise | Token waste; ambiguous commits/PRs |
| Second contract format beside SPEC.md | Agents diverge; /ship and ad-hoc disagree |
| SDD core via sub-agent swarm | Context blow-up; contract mode non-goal |
| Full grill→review chain for a typo | Ceremony > value (violates right-size) |
| Build retries without classifying failure | Silent spec/code divergence |
| Invariant without test | Rule is fiction |
| Adversarial review on trivial changes | Hallucinated flaws; wasted budget |
| Deepen mid-feature under deadline | Churn disguised as refactor |
| Scattered logs per request | Cannot query; debug by grep lottery |
| Stack skills installed but never referenced | Dead weight; confuses agent routing |
| New top-level folders without updating the layout map | Second tree; agents place files at random |
| Organizing large apps only by file type (`hooks/`, `utils/`) | No feature locality; placement fights change |
| Ideal greenfield tree that ignores the repo on disk | Blueprint lies; reviews can't enforce |
| One mega-PR for a multi-layer / AI-sized change | Review quality collapses; use `/stacking-prs` |
| Stack layer over 30 files or multi-concern | Unreviewable; split before `gh stack submit` |

